# A CR in the shebang makes the script unrunnable on Linux/macOS with a
# baffling "env: bash\r: No such file or directory" (or python3\r). Force LF
# everywhere -- demo/bin/git-roost hit exactly this checked out from Windows
# and run under WSL.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# The inverse of the rule above: packaging/git-roost.cmd never runs anywhere
# but cmd.exe, which is the one interpreter here that actually expects CRLF --
# unlike LF-only shebang scripts, an LF-only batch file mostly works by luck of
# cmd.exe's tolerance rather than by contract. Pin it explicitly rather than
# rely on that tolerance.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
